  "_comment": [
    "Per-personality interiority (see DATAPACK.md). 'baselines' is where a villager's disposition axes",
    "rest before the player has done anything; 'stance_bias' is how well a kind of thing the player says",
    "lands on them, added to a dialogue check's score. Baselines clamp to +/-15, stance bias to +/-12,",
    "which is less than one tier margin - personality colours an outcome, it never decides one.",
    "Guardrails: no personality is punished by all ordinary choices, 'sensitive' is not fragile,",
    "'crabby' is not hostile, and every personality has at least one warm route and one honest one."
